      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): catch unhandled rejections in webhook and ingress worker shutdown",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes two channel reliability bugs in the Telegram plugin where shutdown paths can produce unhandled promise rejections, which Node.js terminates the process for by default:\n\n1. **Webhook shutdown**: if `bot.stop()` rejected during abort-triggered shutdown, the rejection was unhandled (`void shutdown()`), crashing the process.\n2. **Ingress worker stop**: `stop()` was not idempotent, so calling it twice could post a second `stop` message and leak a second 15s terminate timer. If `worker.terminate()` rejected, the rejection was unhandled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- **Webhook**: catch shutdown errors in both the pre-aborted path and the abort listener, route them to `runtime.error`, and continue owned cleanup (transport close, status, diagnostics) in a `finally` block even if `bot.stop()` rejects.\n- **Ingress worker**: guard `stop()` with a `stopped` flag for idempotency, catch `postMessage` errors for already-terminated workers, and catch `worker.terminate()` rejections.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo more unhandled rejection crashes during Telegram channel restart or shutdown.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run\n```\n\n```\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  38 passed (38)\n```\n\n### Negative Control Proof\n\n**Webhook shutdown rejection handling**:\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Revert to origin/main version\ngit checkout origin/main -- extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts\n\n# Step 2: Run test - Expected: FAIL with Unhandled Rejection\npnpm test extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run -t \"does not leak unhandled rejections when shutdown throws\"\n```\n\nResult: ❌ **FAILED** - Unhandled Rejection: Error: bot stop failed\n\n```bash\n# Step 3: Restore fix\ngit checkout HEAD -- extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts\n\n# Step 4: Run test - Expected: PASS\npnpm test extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run -t \"does not leak unhandled rejections when shutdown throws\"\n```\n\nResult: ✅ **PASSED** - 1 passed\n\n**Ingress worker stop idempotency**:\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Revert to origin/main version\ngit checkout origin/main -- extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts\n\n# Step 2: Run test - Expected: FAIL\npnpm test extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run\n```\n\nResult: ❌ **FAILED** - AssertionError: expected Promise{…} to be Promise{…} (stop() not idempotent)\n\n```bash\n# Step 3: Restore fix\ngit checkout HEAD -- extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts\n\n# Step 4: Run test - Expected: ALL PASS\npnpm test extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run\n```\n\nResult: ✅ **PASSED** - 2 passed\n\n### Changes\n\n- `extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts`: catch shutdown errors in abort paths, log via `runtime.error`, continue cleanup in `finally`\n- `extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts`: new test for shutdown rejection handling\n- `extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts`: idempotent `stop()` with shared stop promise, catch `postMessage` and `terminate` errors\n- `extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts`: new tests for stop idempotency and terminate rejection handling\n\n---\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
